## Release Anchor and Recovery Gate

Before recommending recovery, rollback, release branching, or final release:

1. Inspect existing **local and remote tags** (`git tag --list`, `git ls-remote --tags origin`).
2. Identify tag category: **baseline**, **RC**, **final release**, or **hotfix** (see [git-tags-and-recovery-runbook.md](../../docs/ops/git-tags-and-recovery-runbook.md)).
3. Prefer **comparison**, **archive**, or **isolated worktree** before altering branches.
4. **Never move** a published tag (DEC-055).
5. **Never recommend** resetting or force-pushing `main` without an approved incident procedure.
6. Distinguish **code recovery** (Git tag) from **database/infrastructure recovery** (operator runbooks).
7. Keep tag **creation and publication human-controlled** — agents do not publish tags unless explicitly instructed.
8. Record newly verified release anchors in `current-state.md` or the release plan when operator confirms.
9. **Git tags do not back up database rows** — a code tag (including `dat-v1-core-baseline-95b833e`) cannot restore deleted organizations, users, or lessons.

Full commands: [git-tags-and-recovery-runbook.md](../../docs/ops/git-tags-and-recovery-runbook.md) — do not duplicate the complete runbook here.

